<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28165" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δουλ-εύω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοῦλος</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be a slave,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.56
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.138
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				777d
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρά τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					18.129
				</span></i>
			: c. acc. cogn., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δουλείαν δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Mem.</u>
					3.12.2
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				183a
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>serve, be subject,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τό τ᾽ ἄρχειν καὶ τὸ δ. δίχα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					927
				</span></i>
			, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ζεύγλαις</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				463
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς ἄρχουσι καὶ τοῖς νόμοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					698b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡδονῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					238e
				</span></i>
			, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. γαστρί, ὕπνῳ, λαγνείᾳ,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				1.6.8
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεναῖς δόξαις</span>
				Polystr.<i><span class="en">
				p.29
			</span></i> W.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ γῇ δ.</span>
			<i>make oneself a slave</i> to one's land, i. e. give up rights
			that one may keep it, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.81
			</span></i>; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. τῇ κτήσει αὐτοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					494d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δουλεύομεν δόξαισιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philem.
					93.8
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. τῷ καιρῷ</span>
			<i>accommodate oneself</i> to the occasion, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.441
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Pall.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdn.
					1.17.6
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>render a service,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PLond.</u>
					5.1727.11
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(vi A. D.)</span>.</div>
